  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Based HIV&amp;AIDS prevention, support and care initiatives project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a one year project designed to consolidate the achievements of the concluded HIV pilot project that was being implemented in the diocese with CAFOD support through Sudan Bishops Regional Secretariat (SCBRS) in the last three years. The review of the previous national HIV programme in the south highlighted the importance of bridging the current gaps in order to strengthen and consolidate on the achievements with more involvement of the diocese.

The project aims at promoting service seeking behaviours in the effort to reduce HIV infections and it&#x2019;s after effects among the communities of Tambura/Yambio diocese and WES in general and, to address issues of sustainability, efficiency and wider coverage of VCT and support group services. The proposed strategic intervention activities will include comprehensive HIV awareness campaigns, strengthening of VCTs &amp; formation of support groups, treatment of opportunistic diseases and establishment of a technical and support staff team to manage and coordinate project activities.

The project targets the host community, returnees, IDPs and refugees from Congo currently in the region as a result of LRA attacks along the borders DRC and Western Equatoria State (Yambio). A total of at least 20,000 people within the wider community of which 50% will be women and youths and 5,000 PLHIV will be reached.</narrative>
  </description>
